      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SPANISH BLAZE (7) settled well back last start and never threatened when 11 lengths from the winner in 11th over 1200m at Ballarat Synthetic. Will appreciate the sharp drop back in company here. Has the ability to put the recent poor run behind him. VICTORY BAY (4) was in the money two starts back at Mt Isa but was unable to repeat the effort last time when eighth, beaten 6 lengths, at Emerald over 1280m. Robert Faehr gets the best out of this eight-year-old gelding. Stepping up a level this time but on his best form he is good enough to take this out. GREEN SHADOWS (2) drifted well back and failed to finish it off last start when tenth, beaten 7 lengths, over 1600m at Birdsville. Ideally placed and is sure to take a ton of beating now third run back. JUNE (6) was beaten 4 lengths into fifth over 1600m at Sunshine Coast two weeks ago. Finds a nice race and can bounce back.",
